      "text": "To find \\( f(3) \\), we start by using the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2. \\]\n\nFirst, substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3(3)^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\tag{1} \\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the original equation:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\tag{2} \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27 \\),\n2. \\( f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12 \\).\n\nWe can solve this system by expressing \\( f(-2) \\) from the second equation and substituting it into the first equation. From the second equation, solve for \\( f(-2) \\):\n\\[ f(-2) = 12 - 2f(3). \\tag{3} \\]\n\nSubstitute equation (3) into the first equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2(12 - 2f(3)) = 27. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 24 - 4f(3) = 27, \\]\n\\[ -3f(3) + 24 = 27, \\]\n\\[ -3f(3) = 3, \\]\n\\[ f(3) = -1. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
